 step('Prove mean preservation from the actual law','The current U acts almost everywhere by the actual reflection F. The independently compiled augmentation invariance gives F#J=J, so change of variables preserves the integral. Conditional expectation preserves the full integral as well. Since J is a probability law, every L2 observable is integrable, and subtraction of actual representatives is legitimate.',r'F_\#J=J,\quad\int Uu\,dJ=\int u\,dJ,\quad\int Pu\,dJ=\int u\,dJ,\quad L^2(J)\subset L^1(J).','  let D :','  let ι :'),
